      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The index-build memory allowance is shared across indexes created by one createIndexes command, separately from WiredTiger cache memory; exceeding the allowance causes temporary files to be used. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/reference/parameters/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4e12d966b816494acc7c852e12e176c502d690105a6393ced9c4f56107a7e49d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b8f4eaa560627ddee46bc481b7f6f7b024984b008dc6bd65e2bb9c6e8d0ecc5",
            "ev:c1565aec862a551791f63106d7d6ccce7e61da502ca4c9426af0f090329f8364"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A createIndexes request consumes one concurrency slot even when it builds multiple indexes; the request shares its memory budget among those indexes. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/parameters.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ec64662acec98abf97f20561998fc2e579b1a8ff4390e7dea0beab431dc28df2",
