    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas maxIndexBuildMemoryUsageMegabytes defaults are M10–M20: 100 MB; M30: 250 MB; M40: 400 MB; M50–M60: 512 MB; M80–M140: 1024 MB; M200+: 2048 MB. The documentation labels tiers as comparable to instance-RAM bands. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/parameters.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:af3d11f4a7b78e01af00c4539d798a38f2963a02f6c796d180c0275e728bd160",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b8f4eaa560627ddee46bc481b7f6f7b024984b008dc6bd65e2bb9c6e8d0ecc5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The generic 200 MB per-createIndexes default is explicitly scoped to self-hosted deployments; it should not replace the Atlas tier table in capacity estimates. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/reference/parameters/",
          "note": null,
